WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.134 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiFTeR: Generating LiDAR Gaussian Fields from Surround-View

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:04.647 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
Cameras.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.886 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
Scene-specific LiDAR reconstruction typically uses real LiDAR

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:15.347 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
observations and optimization for each scene. In contrast, a

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:19.586 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
generated point cloud or range image is not necessarily a

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.965 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
renderable scene representation.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:27.669 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiFTeR explores a combination of camera-conditioned diffusion and

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:31.527 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
Gaussian decoding, aiming to generate a renderable LiDAR

00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:35.179 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
representation while reducing per-scene optimization.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.825 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
During training, frozen variational autoencoders encode six

00:00:40.825 --> 00:00:45.411 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
camera images and ground-truth LiDAR range and intensity. The

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:49.996 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
latent canvas contains one LiDAR slot and six image-condition

00:00:49.996 --> 00:00:50.447 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
slots.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:56.001 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
For generation, the LiDAR slot starts from noise. A multi-view

00:00:56.001 --> 00:01:00.473 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
diffusion transformer uses the camera conditions and iteratively

00:01:00.473 --> 00:01:04.804 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
predicts a LiDAR latent. The current data pipeline still reads

00:01:04.804 --> 00:01:08.437 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiDAR fields for canvas construction and evaluation.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.406 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The resulting latent can be directly decoded by the LiDAR

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:17.404 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
variational autoencoder, or sent through an optional Gaussian

00:01:17.404 --> 00:01:21.534 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
decoding and rendering branch. The U-Net shown in the figure is

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:25.663 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
optional and is not a required step in the current single-frame

00:01:25.663 --> 00:01:26.646 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
inference path.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:32.266 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The Gaussian decoder uses sequence modeling with Mamba two and

00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:36.450 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
self-attention. It predicts per-ray depth, scale, rotation,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.570 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
opacity, intensity, and ray-drop attributes.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.929 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The Gaussian rendering branch produces range, intensity, and

00:01:44.929 --> 00:01:49.138 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
return validity. The rendered observations can then be mapped

00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:53.484 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
back into a sparse point cloud using the LiDAR sensor geometry.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.692 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
Here, a LiFTeR generated point cloud is compared with the

00:01:58.692 --> 00:02:03.093 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
corresponding ground-truth LiDAR. These are qualitative project

00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:06.027 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
examples, not an independent reproduction.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:11.726 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
This same-frame range-view comparison shows the ground truth and

00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:15.449 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiFTeR camera-conditioned result. The other displayed

00:02:15.449 --> 00:02:20.016 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
reconstruction methods use real LiDAR observations; red boxes are

00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:23.177 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
regions highlighted in the original material.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.298 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
For a real-world example, the generated LiDAR points are

00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:32.554 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
projected onto six surrounding camera views. These images are

00:02:32.554 --> 00:02:34.159 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
static project results.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.731 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The real-world example also compares generated and ground-truth

00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:43.934 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
point clouds, allowing their scene structures to be inspected

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:44.830 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
side by side.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.138 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The project further presents a qualitative downstream detection

00:02:50.138 --> 00:02:54.311 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
example, with predicted boxes projected onto the camera view for

00:02:54.311 --> 00:02:56.463 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
generated and ground-truth LiDAR.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:01.934 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
The failure cases show remaining limitations. In this low-light

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:05.994 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
scene, distant structures can be missing or distorted in the

00:03:05.994 --> 00:03:07.483 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
generated point cloud.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:12.911 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiFTeR explores a path from surround-view images to renderable

00:03:12.911 --> 00:03:16.028 line:48% position:50%,center size:60% align:center
LiDAR representations. Thank you for watching.
